 \"custom indexes\" can mean several things.  If it means, you just want to create an index explicitly, you just use op.create_index().   If it means, you want to create an index that makes use of some unsupported syntax, like a Postgresql functional index, you write out the \"CREATE INDEX\" statement as a string and invoke it via op.execute().\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882278","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/81#issuecomment-441882278","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/81","id":441882278,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTg4MjI3OA==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node